# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EnglishWithDan — HTTP response headers for the Render Static Site
# (Netlify/Render `_headers` syntax: a path line, then indented `Name: value`
# lines; applies to the matched paths of THIS static deploy — the public
# pages AND the /admin SPA served from the same bucket).
#
# BUG-A04: the static frontend was shipping only `x-content-type-options`.
# The Express API is already fully hardened via Helmet; these bring the
# pages that hold the JWT (in localStorage) up to the same baseline —
# clickjacking, referrer, transport, and a Content-Security-Policy.
#
# CSP note: `script-src`/`style-src` keep `'unsafe-inline'` because the
# pages use inline <script> blocks and ~1000 inline on* handlers (removing
# them is a large refactor, tracked separately). The real protection here
# is `connect-src` (an XSS-injected script still can't exfiltrate a stolen
# token to an arbitrary host), plus `frame-ancestors`, `object-src`,
# `base-uri`. No `'unsafe-eval'` — nothing in the codebase needs it.
#
# If a page breaks after deploy, the browser console names the exact
# blocked directive; widen that one line (or delete this file to fully
# revert). Smoke-test after deploy: load index / login / dashboard /
# reading / listening / speaking (mic) / writing (Google-Docs preview
# iframe) / dictation / admin, watch the console for CSP violations.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(self), payment=(), usb=(), accelerometer=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), browsing-topics=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' data: blob: https:; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; frame-src https://docs.google.com https://docs.googleusercontent.com; connect-src 'self' https://englishwithdan.onrender.com wss://englishwithdan.onrender.com https://res.cloudinary.com https://api.dictionaryapi.dev https://translate.googleapis.com https://translate.google.com https://api.mymemory.translated.net

# ── Caching ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HTML must revalidate on every load so a new deploy's updated
# `<script src="...?v=YYYYMMDD">` tags are picked up immediately — without
# this, a browser holding a cached .html keeps requesting the OLD asset
# versions and features silently break until the student hard-refreshes
# (Ctrl+Shift+R).
/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/admin/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# JS/CSS were left on the CDN's default long cache on the theory that their
# `?v=` (or admin build hash) always changes on release — in practice a
# shared file touched without remembering to bump every page's `?v=`, or two
# pages loading the same script with different query strings, meant a stale
# copy could keep being served from a browser's disk cache with NO network
# request at all, invisible until someone hard-refreshed. `no-cache` forces
# a revalidation request every load (a fast 304 when nothing changed) so the
# actual file content decides freshness, not whether a human remembered to
# edit a version string. The one exception is /admin/assets/* — Vite content-
# hashes those filenames, so a changed file is a NEW url by construction and
# an old one never needs to be re-fetched; those keep the long default cache
# for that reason, and still update immediately since /admin/ (its
# referencing index.html) is no-cache above.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/admin/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
